{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T10:50:35.368Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The task is the binary-formatting function. I’m using the prompt’s direct formulation—Python’s `bin`, a slice removing `0b`, and the required `db` framing—because it keeps both the implementation and the semantics small enough for a symbolic proof over every non-negative integer, not just the two examples.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T10:50:35.371Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0d789be7aff6577b016a60a0785ad88196aced4c07f75f715c","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The task is the binary-formatting function. I’m using the prompt’s direct formulation—Python’s `bin`, a slice removing `0b`, and the required `db` framing—because it keeps both the implementation and the semantics small enough for a symbolic proof over every non-negative integer, not just the two examples."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f8971-80db-7f22-b37a-c8cc019342df"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T10:50:56.489Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0d789be7aff6577b016a60a07b543c8196b1ec41b273f65e83","status":"completed","call_id":"call_iu08yKYuuOZLVfzzPeQzubuB","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /work/solution.py\\n+def decimal_to_binary(decimal):\\n+    return \\\"db\\\" + bin(decimal)[2:] + \\\"db\\\"\\n*** Add File: /work/semantic.k\\n+requires \\\"domains.k\\\"\\n+\\n+module SEMANTIC-SYNTAX\\n+  imports INT-SYNTAX\\n+  imports STRING-SYNTAX\\n+\\n+  syntax Program ::= \\\"Module\\\" \\\"(\\\" Stmt \\\")\\\" [symbol(moduleProgram)]\\n+\\n+  syntax Stmt ::= \\\"FuncDef\\\" \\\"(\\\" String \\\",\\\" Params \\\",\\\" Stmt \\\")\\\"\\n+                [symbol(functionDefinition)]\\n+                | \\\"Return\\\" \\\"(\\\" Expr \\\")\\\" [symbol(returnStatement)]\\n+\\n+  syntax Params ::= \\\"Params\\\" \\\"(\\\" String \\\")\\\" [symbol(parameters)]\\n+\\n+  syntax Expr ::= \\\"Int\\\" \\\"(\\\" Int \\\")\\\" [symbol(integerExpression)]\\n+                | \\\"Str\\\" \\\"(\\\" String \\\")\\\" [symbol(stringExpression)]\\n+                | \\\"Name\\\" \\\"(\\\" String \\\")\\\" [symbol(nameExpression)]\\n+                | \\\"BinOp\\\" \\\"(\\\" String \\\",\\\" Expr \\\",\\\" Expr \\\")\\\"\\n+                  [symbol(binaryExpression)]\\n+                | \\\"Call\\\" \\\"(\\\" Expr \\\",\\\" Expr \\\")\\\" [symbol(callExpression)]\\n+                | \\\"Subscript\\\" \\\"(\\\" Expr \\\",\\\" Slice \\\")\\\"\\n+                  [symbol(subscriptExpression)]\\n+\\n+  syntax Slice ::= \\\"Slice\\\" \\\"(\\\" Bound \\\",\\\" Bound \\\",\\\" Bound \\\")\\\"\\n+                   [symbol(sliceExpression)]\\n+  syntax Bound ::= Expr | \\\"NoBound\\\" [symbol(noBound)]\\n+endmodule\\n+\\n+module SEMANTIC\\n+  imports SEMANTIC-SYNTAX\\n+  imports INT\\n+  imports STRING\\n+\\n+  syntax Env ::= \\\"bind\\\" \\\"(\\\" String \\\",\\\" Int \\\")\\\" [symbol(bind)]\\n+\\n+  syntax Val ::= \\\"intVal\\\" \\\"(\\\" Int \\\")\\\" [symbol(intVal)]\\n+               | \\\"strVal\\\" \\\"(\\\" String \\\")\\\" [symbol(strVal)]\\n+\\n+  syntax Val ::= eval(Expr, Env) [function]\\n+               | addValues(Val, Val) [function]\\n+               | callBin(Val) [function]\\n+               | suffixFrom(Val, Int) [function]\\n+\\n+  syntax String ::= binDigits(Int) [function]\\n+\\n+  configuration\\n+    <python>\\n+      <k> $PGM:Program </k>\\n+      <arg> $ARG:Int </arg>\\n+      <result> .K </result>\\n+    </python>\\n+\\n+  rule <k>\\n+         Module(\\n+           FuncDef(\\\"decimal_to_binary\\\", Params(\\\"decimal\\\"), Return(E))\\n+         )\\n+       => .K\\n+       </k>\\n+       <arg> I </arg>\\n+       <result> .K => eval(E, bind(\\\"decimal\\\", I)) </result>\\n+\\n+  rule eval(Int(I), _) => intVal(I)\\n+  rule eval(Str(S), _) => strVal(S)\\n+  rule eval(Name(X), bind(X, I)) => intVal(I)\\n+  rule eval(BinOp(\\\"+\\\", LEFT, RIGHT), RHO)\\n+    => addValues(eval(LEFT, RHO), eval(RIGHT, RHO))\\n+  rule eval(Call(Name(\\\"bin\\\"), ARG), RHO) => callBin(eval(ARG, RHO))\\n+  rule eval(Subscript(BASE, Slice(Int(START), NoBound, NoBound)), RHO)\\n+    => suffixFrom(eval(BASE, RHO), START)\\n+\\n+  rule addValues(intVal(I), intVal(J)) => intVal(I +Int J)\\n+  rule addValues(strVal(S), strVal(T)) => strVal(S +String T)\\n+\\n+  rule callBin(intVal(I)) => strVal(\\\"0b\\\" +String binDigits(I))\\n+    requires I >=Int 0\\n+\\n+  rule suffixFrom(strVal(\\\"0b\\\" +String S), 2) => strVal(S)\\n+\\n+  rule binDigits(I) => Int2String(I)\\n+    requires 0 <=Int I andBool I <Int 2\\n+  rule binDigits(I) => binDigits(I /Int 2) +String Int2String(I %Int 2)\\n+    requires I >=Int 2\\n+endmodule\\n*** Add File: /work/verification.k\\n+requires \\\"semantic.k\\\"\\n+\\n+module VERIFICATION\\n+  imports SEMANTIC\\n+\\n+  // A mathematical presentation of the required wrapper around the usual\\n+  // base-two digit expansion.  Keeping it separate from expression evaluation\\n+  // makes the reachability claim state the contract rather than an AST result.\\n+  syntax String ::= decimalToBinarySpec(Int) [function]\\n+\\n+  rule decimalToBinarySpec(I)\\n+    => \\\"db\\\" +String binDigits(I) +String \\\"db\\\"\\n+    requires I >=Int 0\\n+endmodule\\n*** Add File: /work/spec.k\\n+requires \\\"verification.k\\\"\\n+\\n+module SPEC\\n+  imports VERIFICATION\\n+\\n+  claim\\n+    <k>\\n+      Module(\\n+        FuncDef(\\n+          \\\"decimal_to_binary\\\",\\n+          Params(\\\"decimal\\\"),\\n+          Return(\\n+            BinOp(\\n+              \\\"+\\\",\\n+              BinOp(\\n+                \\\"+\\\",\\n+                Str(\\\"db\\\"),\\n+                Subscript(\\n+                  Call(Name(\\\"bin\\\"), Name(\\\"decimal\\\")),\\n+                  Slice(Int(2), NoBound, NoBound)\\n+                )\\n+              ),\\n+              Str(\\\"db\\\")\\n+            )\\n+          )\\n+        )\\n+      )\\n+    => .K\\n+    </k>\\n+    <arg> I:Int </arg>\\n+    <result> .K => strVal(decimalToBinarySpec(I)) </result>\\n+    requires I >=Int 0\\n+\\n+  claim\\n+    <k>\\n+      Module(\\n+        FuncDef(\\n+          \\\"decimal_to_binary\\\",\\n+          Params(\\\"decimal\\\"),\\n+          Return(\\n+            BinOp(\\n+              \\\"+\\\",\\n+              BinOp(\\n+                \\\"+\\\",\\n+                Str(\\\"db\\\"),\\n+                Subscript(\\n+                  Call(Name(\\\"bin\\\"), Name(\\\"decimal\\\")),\\n+                  Slice(Int(2), NoBound, NoBound)\\n+                )\\n+              ),\\n+              Str(\\\"db\\\")\\n+            )\\n+          )\\n+        )\\n+      )\\n+    => .K\\n+    </k>\\n+    <arg> 15 </arg>\\n+    <result> .K => strVal(\\\"db1111db\\\") </result>\\n+\\n+  claim\\n+    <k>\\n+      Module(\\n+        FuncDef(\\n+          \\\"decimal_to_binary\\\",\\n+          Params(\\\"decimal\\\"),\\n+          Return(\\n+            BinOp(\\n+              \\\"+\\\",\\n+              BinOp(\\n+                \\\"+\\\",\\n+                Str(\\\"db\\\"),\\n+                Subscript(\\n+                  Call(Name(\\\"bin\\\"), Name(\\\"decimal\\\")),\\n+                  Slice(Int(2), NoBound, NoBound)\\n+                )\\n+              ),\\n+              Str(\\\"db\\\")\\n+            )\\n+          )\\n+        )\\n+      )\\n+    => .K\\n+    </k>\\n+    <arg> 32 </arg>\\n+    <result> .K => strVal(\\\"db100000db\\\") </result>\\n+endmodule\\n*** Add File: /work/prove.sh\\n+#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n+set -euo pipefail\\n+\\n+python3 py2mpy.py solution.py > solution.mpy\\n+kompile semantic.k --backend haskell --output-definition .kbuild\\n+krun solution.mpy --definition .kbuild -cARG=0\\n+krun solution.mpy --definition .kbuild -cARG=15\\n+krun solution.mpy --definition .kbuild -cARG=32\\n+kprove spec.k --definition .kbuild\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f8971-80db-7f22-b37a-c8cc019342df"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T10:50:56.508Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"patch_apply_end","call_id":"exec-9cb3fdbc-a04b-418f-abc5-c6b0c08d04a9","turn_id":"019f8971-80db-7f22-b37a-c8cc019342df","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /work/solution.py\nA /work/semantic.k\nA /work/verification.k\nA /work/spec.k\nA /work/prove.sh\n","stderr":"","success":true,"changes":{"/work/semantic.k":{"type":"add","content":"requires \"domains.k\"\n\nmodule SEMANTIC-SYNTAX\n  imports INT-SYNTAX\n  imports STRING-SYNTAX\n\n  syntax Program ::= \"Module\" \"(\" Stmt \")\" [symbol(moduleProgram)]\n\n  syntax Stmt ::= \"FuncDef\" \"(\" String \",\" Params \",\" Stmt \")\"\n                [symbol(functionDefinition)]\n                | \"Return\" \"(\" Expr \")\" [symbol(returnStatement)]\n\n  syntax Params ::= \"Params\" \"(\" String \")\" [symbol(parameters)]\n\n  syntax Expr ::= \"Int\" \"(\" Int \")\" [symbol(integerExpression)]\n                | \"Str\" \"(\" String \")\" [symbol(stringExpression)]\n                | \"Name\" \"(\" String \")\" [symbol(nameExpression)]\n                | \"BinOp\" \"(\" String \",\" Expr \",\" Expr \")\"\n                  [symbol(binaryExpression)]\n                | \"Call\" \"(\" Expr \",\" Expr \")\" [symbol(callExpression)]\n                | \"Subscript\" \"(\" Expr \",\" Slice \")\"\n                  [symbol(subscriptExpression)]\n\n  syntax Slice ::= \"Slice\" \"(\" Bound \",\" Bound \",\" Bound \")\"\n                   [symbol(sliceExpression)]\n  syntax Bound ::= Expr | \"NoBound\" [symbol(noBound)]\nendmodule\n\nmodule SEMANTIC\n  imports SEMANTIC-SYNTAX\n  imports INT\n  imports STRING\n\n  syntax Env ::= \"bind\" \"(\" String \",\" Int \")\" [symbol(bind)]\n\n  syntax Val ::= \"intVal\" \"(\" Int \")\" [symbol(intVal)]\n               | \"strVal\" \"(\" String \")\" [symbol(strVal)]\n\n  syntax Val ::= eval(Expr, Env) [function]\n               | addValues(Val, Val) [function]\n               | callBin(Val) [function]\n               | suffixFrom(Val, Int) [function]\n\n  syntax String ::= binDigits(Int) [function]\n\n  configuration\n    <python>\n      <k> $PGM:Program </k>\n      <arg> $ARG:Int </arg>\n      <result> .K </result>\n    </python>\n\n  rule <k>\n         Module(\n           FuncDef(\"decimal_to_binary\", Params(\"decimal\"), Return(E))\n         )\n       => .K\n       </k>\n       <arg> I </arg>\n       <result> .K => eval(E, bind(\"decimal\", I)) </result>\n\n  rule eval(Int(I), _) => intVal(I)\n  rule eval(Str(S), _) => strVal(S)\n  rule eval(Name(X), bind(X, I)) => intVal(I)\n  rule eval(BinOp(\"+\", LEFT, RIGHT), RHO)\n    => addValues(eval(LEFT, RHO), eval(RIGHT, RHO))\n  rule eval(Call(Name(\"bin\"), ARG), RHO) => callBin(eval(ARG, RHO))\n  rule eval(Subscript(BASE, Slice(Int(START), NoBound, NoBound)), RHO)\n    => suffixFrom(eval(BASE, RHO), START)\n\n  rule addValues(intVal(I), intVal(J)) => intVal(I +Int J)\n  rule addValues(strVal(S), strVal(T)) => strVal(S +String T)\n\n  rule callBin(intVal(I)) => strVal(\"0b\" +String binDigits(I))\n    requires I >=Int 0\n\n  rule suffixFrom(strVal(\"0b\" +String S), 2) => strVal(S)\n\n  rule binDigits(I) => Int2String(I)\n    requires 0 <=Int I andBool I <Int 2\n  rule binDigits(I) => binDigits(I /Int 2) +String Int2String(I %Int 2)\n    requires I >=Int 2\nendmodule\n"},"/work/verification.k":{"type":"add","content":"requires \"semantic.k\"\n\nmodule VERIFICATION\n  imports SEMANTIC\n\n  // A mathematical presentation of the required wrapper around the usual\n  // base-two digit expansion.  Keeping it separate from expression evaluation\n  // makes the reachability claim state the contract rather than an AST result.\n  syntax String ::= decimalToBinarySpec(Int) [function]\n\n  rule decimalToBinarySpec(I)\n    => \"db\" +String binDigits(I) +String \"db\"\n    requires I >=Int 0\nendmodule\n"},"/work/solution.py":{"type":"add","content":"def decimal_to_binary(decimal):\n    return \"db\" + bin(decimal)[2:] + \"db\"\n"},"/work/prove.sh":{"type":"add","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\npython3 py2mpy.py solution.py > solution.mpy\nkompile semantic.k --backend haskell --output-definition .kbuild\nkrun solution.mpy --definition .kbuild -cARG=0\nkrun solution.mpy --definition .kbuild -cARG=15\nkrun solution.mpy --definition .kbuild -cARG=32\nkprove spec.k --definition .kbuild\n"},"/work/spec.k":{"type":"add","content":"requires \"verification.k\"\n\nmodule SPEC\n  imports VERIFICATION\n\n  claim\n    <k>\n      Module(\n        FuncDef(\n          \"decimal_to_binary\",\n          Params(\"decimal\"),\n          Return(\n            BinOp(\n              \"+\",\n              BinOp(\n                \"+\",\n                Str(\"db\"),\n                Subscript(\n                  Call(Name(\"bin\"), Name(\"decimal\")),\n                  Slice(Int(2), NoBound, NoBound)\n                )\n              ),\n              Str(\"db\")\n            )\n          )\n        )\n      )\n    => .K\n    </k>\n    <arg> I:Int </arg>\n    <result> .K => strVal(decimalToBinarySpec(I)) </result>\n    requires I >=Int 0\n\n  claim\n    <k>\n      Module(\n        FuncDef(\n          \"decimal_to_binary\",\n          Params(\"decimal\"),\n          Return(\n            BinOp(\n              \"+\",\n              BinOp(\n                \"+\",\n                Str(\"db\"),\n                Subscript(\n                  Call(Name(\"bin\"), Name(\"decimal\")),\n                  Slice(Int(2), NoBound, NoBound)\n                )\n              ),\n              Str(\"db\")\n            )\n          )\n        )\n      )\n    => .K\n    </k>\n    <arg> 15 </arg>\n    <result> .K => strVal(\"db1111db\") </result>\n\n  claim\n    <k>\n      Module(\n        FuncDef(\n          \"decimal_to_binary\",\n          Params(\"decimal\"),\n          Return(\n            BinOp(\n              \"+\",\n              BinOp(\n                \"+\",\n                Str(\"db\"),\n                Subscript(\n                  Call(Name(\"bin\"), Name(\"decimal\")),\n                  Slice(Int(2), NoBound, NoBound)\n                )\n              ),\n              Str(\"db\")\n            )\n          )\n        )\n      )\n    => .K\n    </k>\n    <arg> 32 </arg>\n    <result> .K => strVal(\"db100000db\") </result>\nendmodule\n"}},"status":"completed"}}
